From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:43:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] asahi: separate G16 materialization choice in Gallium disk
 cache

Retain a reliable opt-out for OpenGL as well as Vulkan when process flags change.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_disk_cache.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_disk_cache.c b/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_disk_cache.c
index aec17543fa5..5c3718c4c36 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_disk_cache.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_disk_cache.c
@@ -250,6 +250,8 @@ agx_disk_cache_init(struct agx_screen *screen)
    _mesa_sha1_format(timestamp, id_sha1);
 
    uint64_t driver_flags = screen->dev.debug;
+   if (screen->dev.chip == AGX_CHIP_G16G && agx_g16_shared_nz_enabled())
+      driver_flags |= UINT64_C(1) << 63;
    screen->disk_cache = disk_cache_create(renderer, timestamp, driver_flags);
 #endif
 }
-- 
